--
Class-template partial specialization keyed on a nested class-template-id
(`base<holder<T>>`, the libstdc++ `allocator_traits<allocator<T>>` shape),
N5008 [temp.spec.partial.match]/2.  When the member is named through a
namespace-scope qualified-id (`base<holder<int>>::cp`), the nested template-id
argument `holder<int>` must be elaborated so the partial specialization is
selected (and instantiated to completion) rather than falling back to the
body-less primary template.  [temp.inst]/2, [temp.spec.general]/7.
See doc/architectural/cpp-requires-expression-support.md.
